# Windows runners check out with core.autocrlf=true, which rewrites LF to CRLF in
# the working tree. gofmt then reports every converted file as unformatted, so
# the Go job failed on Windows and only there. Go source is LF in the index and
# must stay LF in the working tree on every platform.
*.go text eol=lf

# Same reasoning for the other files a tool compares byte for byte: the
# workflows and configs are read by actionlint and oxlint, and a checksum or a
# fixture that changes shape per platform is a bug waiting to happen.
*.yml text eol=lf
*.yaml text eol=lf
*.json text eol=lf
*.ts text eol=lf
*.tsx text eol=lf
*.sh text eol=lf
